  "summary": "Three November 2026 preprints apply wavefunction and quantum-geometric quantities to Thouless pumps, Chern flat bands and helicoidal metrics.",
  "synthesis": "The three preprints share a focus on quantities defined by the wavefunction and its geometry rather than by band energies alone. Pseudo-entropy in the Rice-Mele model under Thouless pumping and in the open Kitaev chain depends on the reference state and the subsystem partition, so it probes the state beyond the spectrum. In a Chern flat band, single-site DMFT with Hubbard interaction on overcomplete coherent orbitals yields a Mott transition tuned by the Berry curvature fraction, accompanied by emergent heavy fermions. A scalar Schrödinger particle in a helicoidal metric within a hard-wall cylinder shows time-reversal degeneracy, twist-dependent avoided crossings and twist-activated dipole transitions, linking geometric twist to spectral and optical response. The dominant thread is the role of quantum geometry in tuning topological and correlated phases; the helicoidal-metric study is the least direct fit, as it treats a single particle in curved geometry rather than lattice band topology.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
